{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":241431,"ns":0,"title":"Chirp Z-transform","extract":"The chirp Z-transform (CZT) is a generalization of the discrete Fourier transform (DFT).  While the DFT samples the Z plane at uniformly-spaced points along the unit circle, the chirp Z-transform samples along spiral arcs in the Z-plane, corresponding to straight lines in the S plane.","description":"Mathematical algorithm","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}